Subject: FreeBSD 6.4 Alpha doesn't see hard disk on DS10L
Message-ID: <COL101-W1768638959BFBE1A403EEEE6100@phx.gbl>


I had no problem installing Linux on a DS10L from local CD-ROM.


FreeBSD 6.4 boots but doesn't see the hard drive.

Setup gets to the part about partitioning and says there are no disks.

Advise?

(I realize -- development is stopped here.)

Thanks,
 - Jay
 		 	   		  
From lausts at acm.org  Sat Dec 11 14:32:56 2010
From: lausts at acm.org (Thomas Laus)
Date: Sat Dec 11 14:32:59 2010
Subject: FreeBSD 6.4 Alpha doesn't see hard disk on DS10L
In-Reply-To: <COL101-W1768638959BFBE1A403EEEE6100@phx.gbl>
References: <COL101-W1768638959BFBE1A403EEEE6100@phx.gbl>
Message-ID: <4D034185.3540.91DAD@lausts.acm.org>

> I had no problem installing Linux on a DS10L from local CD-ROM.
> FreeBSD 6.4 boots but doesn't see the hard drive.
> Setup gets to the part about partitioning and says there are no disks.
> Advise?
> (I realize -- development is stopped here.)
> 
Most of the time it is because another operating system, especially VMS, was 
used on the hard drive before.  I always do a 'DD if=/dev/zero bs=1M 
count=1000' on any hard drive that is new to my Alpha.  Boot your Alpha from 
a fixit image and wipe the beginning of the previously used hard drive.

Tom
